Queue using Two Stacks

Problem

The goal is to implement a queue using only two stacks. Since a queue follows FIFO (First In, First Out) and a stack follows LIFO (Last In, First Out), the challenge is to maintain the correct order of elements.

Approach

I used the costly enqueue approach. Before inserting a new element, I move all elements from Stack 1 to Stack 2. Then I push the new element into Stack 1 and move all elements back from Stack 2 to Stack 1. This keeps the front of the queue at the top of Stack 1, so the pop operation becomes simple.

Complexity

Push (Enqueue): O(n)

Pop (Dequeue): O(1)

Front: O(1)

Space Complexity: O(n)

Learning

This problem helped me understand that one data structure can be implemented using another. I also learned that there can be more than one valid solution for the same problem, with different time complexity trade-offs. More importantly, I understood the logic behind the implementation instead of just memorizing the code.
